    10	## 1. The question
    11	
    12	Can a standard, well-tuned projection ROM with classical hyper-reduction — POD-LSPG with ECSW or with Q-DEIM — match
    13	or beat the off-mesh coordinate-bank ROM ("ours") on viscous Burgers 2D and 3D, at equal tuning budget, in online time
    14	per query and in E0 error? This is **H-base** (PLAN-v2 §1). It can falsify the paper's framing: if a POD baseline is
    15	both faster and more accurate than a qualified configuration of ours on the same mesh, the claim is withdrawn for that
    16	cell.
    17	
    18	H-base is evaluated **per dimension and mesh**, against **each numerically qualified configuration of ours** on that
    19	mesh (priority-1 lane `jcp-p1-scaling` in 2D, `jcp-speed3d` in 3D; §8).
    20	
    21	## 2. Problem, cohorts, references, scoring
    22	
    23	- **PDE.** $u_t + u\sum_{a=1}^{d} \partial_a u = \nu \Delta u$ on
    24	  $(0,1)^d$, $u=0$ on the walls, $t\in[0,0.25]$, outputs at $t_k = 0.05k$, $k=0..5$.
    25	  - 2D: Gaussian bump $(c_x,c_y,w,a,\nu)$, IC `engines.initial(L, desc)`, $\nu\in[0.01,0.1]$ log-uniform.
    26	  - 3D: 1–3 masked blobs (`common.table`, IC `common.initial_interior(n, tab, j)`), $\nu\in[0.01,0.1]$.
    27	- **Meshes (C3-minimal).** 2D $L\in\{256, 1024\}$ intervals per axis (state $(L-1)^2$); 3D $L=64$ (state $63^3$,
    28	  i.e. the $65^3$-node mesh of ours). 2D $4096^2$ and 3D $L>64$ are **deferred to C3-full** (§12): the POD snapshot
    29	  matrix alone would be $576\cdot12\cdot4095^2\cdot8\,\mathrm{B}\approx 0.93$ TB in 2D.
    30	- **Cohorts** (development/validation only; never test as selection, never sealed/OOD):
    31	  - **Selection cohort** (baseline tuning): 2D `dev6`; 3D `923801` cases 0–5.
    32	  - **Verdict cohort** (H-base): 2D `dev6`+`val32` (38 cases); 3D `923801` all 64 cases. These are the cohorts on which
    33	    our configurations were selected and qualified (combined/P1/speed3d), so both methods are compared in-sample on the
