    45	## 3. The baselines
    46	
    47	### 3.1 The full-order operator the baselines project
    48	
    49	A projection ROM inherits its full-order discretisation. The baselines project the **central-difference** FOM of the
    50	E0 references (`refcore.adv_central`, `refcore.lap`, arithmetic identical), on the baseline's own mesh $L$:
    51	
    52	$$F_h(u) = N_h(u) - \nu\,\Delta_h u,\qquad N_h(u)_i = u_i \sum_{a=1}^{d}\frac{u_{i+e_a}-u_{i-e_a}}{2h},$$
    53	
    54	$\Delta_h$ the 5-/7-point Laplacian, zero ghost values at the walls. This is the stronger of the two FD operators in the
    55	repository (speed3d f1, in-job and unaudited: central-CN median 0.16–0.47 % at $64^3$ against upwind 3.7–4.1 %). The
    56	sign-upwind operator is **not** used (first-order; it would hand the baseline a floor of several percent). A
    57	pseudo-spectral FOM is not projected: its nonlinear term is global, so no sampling-based hyper-reduction applies.
    58	**Baseline floor.** The un-reduced FOM with the same operator, mesh, scheme and Δt is run on the verdict cohort and
    59	scored against E0; it is the error floor any POD-LSPG of that FOM approaches as $r\to n$, and is reported beside every
    60	baseline number.
