   309	## 13. Deliverables
   310	
   311	`DESIGN.md` (+ amendments), `audits/` (every Codex file), `runs/GPU-LEDGER.json`, `runs/EXPORT.json` (per pair: picks,
   312	labels, intervals, offline costs; per configuration: Q1, errors, times), `make_report.py` → `report.md` with plots:
   313	baseline fronts against ours per cell (time vs worst error, with Q1 failures shown separately), POD singular values and
   314	projection floors, ECSW/Q-DEIM sample count vs error, native vs common solver, offline-cost bars. Every number in the
   315	report is generated. Glossary at the end.
   316	
   317	## 14. Appendix: C3-full (priority 4), design sketch only — not implemented in phase I
   318	
   319	- **GNAT** (Carlberg et al. 2013): residual and Jacobian gappy POD with oversampled sample mesh ($n_s > n_r \ge r$),
   320	  Q-DEIM/greedy sampling; reuses §3.4's stencil machinery.
   321	- **POD + exact tensor:** the quadratic advection term precomputed as $T_{ijk} = \phi_i^\top(\phi_j\odot D\phi_k)$ for
   322	  the central operator ($O(r^3)$ storage, exact, no sampling); feasible for r ≤ 256 (2D: 128 MB at r = 256).
   323	- **Best-practice EQ on our bank:** NNLS empirical quadrature (Yano/Patera style) on the bank's weak residual with
   324	  the same candidate/target recipe as §3.4, replacing the classical rules.
   325	- **Continuum ECSW:** weights on the off-mesh points of ours rather than mesh nodes.
   326	- **CROM-style sampler:** a continuous reduced-order model's sampled-point network (Chen et al. 2023) with the same
   327	  training data.
   328	- **Larger meshes:** 2D $4096^2$ and 3D $L\in\{128,256\}$ via a streaming randomised range finder (two passes,
   329	  regenerating trajectories) instead of the in-memory method of snapshots.
