   333	## Amendment A1 (2026-10-18) — answers to Codex design audit 1 (`audits/codex-design-1.md`, verdict WRONG)
   334	
   335	Each item below replaces the text it names; where A1 and the sections above differ, A1 governs. Item numbers are the
   336	audit's.
   337	
   338	**A1.1 (items 1, 2) Residual and Jacobian, explicit.** The baselines solve weighted strong-residual LSPG ("ECSW" names
   339	the sampling-and-weighting construction; no energy-conservation property is claimed for this Burgers discretisation).
   340	With $u=\Phi_r c$ and $s(u)_i=\tfrac L2\sum_a(u_{i+e_a}-u_{i-e_a})$,
   341	$$J(c)=\partial_c\mathcal R_n(\Phi_rc)=\Big[a_0 I+\Delta t\,b_0\big(\operatorname{diag}(s(u))+\operatorname{diag}(u)\,D_h-\nu\Delta_h\big)\Big]\Phi_r,$$
   342	$D_h$ the central derivative-sum operator ($s(u)=D_hu$). The same expression (restricted to rows, times $\sqrt{\xi}$) is
   343	used for ECSW online rows and for ECSW training contributions; G-fd checks it.
   344	
   345	**A1.2 (item 3) Q-DEIM objective without truncation.** The SVD with a singular-value cut-off is withdrawn. Offline, the
   346	Householder QR $B=[\Phi_r,\ \Delta_h\Phi_r,\ U_p]=Q_BR_B$ is formed in f64 (Householder QR is column-wise backward
   347	stable, so the very different column scales of $\Phi_r$ and $\Delta_h\Phi_r$ are harmless); online
   348	$\hat r_n(c)=R_Bz(c)$, so $\|\hat r_n(c)\|=\|Bz(c)\|$ exactly for every $c$ and no linear term is approximated. $R_B$ is
   349	never inverted, so rank deficiency of $B$ does not matter. The DEIM approximation is the only approximation; G-fd
   350	compares $\|R_Bz\|$ and $J^\top\hat r$ with the independently assembled full-field DEIM residual
   351	$\Phi_r(\cdot)-\Delta t\nu\Delta_h\Phi_r(\cdot)+U_p(P^\top U_p)^{-1}(\cdot)$ and its gradient on random states,
   352	including a near-cancellation state (the residual at a converged step).
   353	
   354	**A1.3 (items 4, 5) Snapshot provenance, restated.**
   355	- Reused: the **parameter draws** of the banks' training (2D `sample_params(0, 576)`, 3D `table(923701, 1536)`). Not
   356	  reused: the banks' **trajectory generator** (sign-upwind BE, fields never stored) and, in 2D, the bank's **state
   357	  selection** (all 51 states of 576 trajectories, of which all states with step ≤ 5 plus a random sample, 16,384 in total;
