   396	**A1.7 (item 9) Q1 restated exactly.** Distance = $\max_{k\ge1}\|F_k-F_k^{\rm tight}\|/n_0$ on the scoring lattice,
   397	$n_0$ = the canonical physical IC norm on the lattice (the E0 metric's $n_0$; checked equal to the store's
   398	`judge.n0` to 1e-12), not the POD-projected IC. Tight and tighter anchors must themselves be **valid** (every step
   399	stationary at their level or at residual tolerance, finite, no damping saturation); an invalid anchor makes the
