  1366	## Amendment A23 (2026-10-18) — smk2 result and the "optimum before target" rule
  1367	
  1368	smk2 (job 5422908, H200, 38:02) passed every acceptance gate under the staged checker except
  1369	`2d_L1024|ecsw-smoke-rank`: the 2D r = 128 NNLS path terminated at a KKT-certified NNLS optimum (reason `kkt`, 1,677
  1370	iterations, 13 bans, support below 16r = 2,048) after reaching 2r, 4r and 8r (training residuals 1.7e-4, 6.7e-5,
  1371	2.5e-6), so the 16r checkpoint did not exist and the staged checker (which required all four) failed. This is not a
  1372	construction defect: the training problem was solved exactly with fewer points than the target.
  1373	**Rule (A23):** when a path ends at a KKT-certified optimum (both KKT inequalities, A5.2) before reaching a support
  1374	target, that target's configuration **is the optimum** (actual support and residual reported, flagged `optimum`), not a
  1375	construction failure; for runs made before this rule (smk2) the absent checkpoint is accepted under the same condition.
  1376	Acceptance of smk2 is recomputed with the amended checker (`runs/smk2/ACCEPTANCE-A23.json`); the staged result
  1377	(ALL = false, this gate only) is kept unchanged beside it. smk2 ran the A17 full-QR NNLS; the production algorithm is the
  1378	A20/A22 updating QR, equal to it by the binding gate G-nnls.
  1379	
