   966	## Amendment A8 (2026-10-18) — solver tolerances and anchors, from the local CPU dry run (no verdict data)
   967	
   968	Evidence (local CPU dry run of `smoke.py` at reduced size: 2D L = 256, r = 16, 24 training trajectories; a code-path
   969	test, not a result): with ours' production stopping rule γ ≤ 1e-3, the native Gauss–Newton stopped after one iteration
   970	per step and its rollouts were 2.4–3.3e-4 from the tight solve (Q1 bar 2.5e-4); the common LM stopped at the
   971	extrapolated predictor on 40 % of steps (1.3–1.7e-4); and an LM (Cholesky normal equations) **tighter** anchor on an
   972	ECSW problem stalled at γ ≈ 2e-8 > 1e-8 (round-off of the squared normal equations), making the anchor invalid.
   973	
   974	**A8.1 Native production tolerance.** The native Gauss–Newton (QR, backtracking) stops at γ ≤ **1e-6** (residual
   975	criterion unchanged). Ours' γ ≤ 1e-3 is a setting tuned for ours' LM with a quadratic-extrapolation predictor; the
   976	native solver is entitled to its own convergence rule, and Gauss–Newton's quadratic convergence makes the extra
   977	iteration cheap. The common solver keeps ours' settings exactly (γ ≤ 1e-3), as an ablation. Q1's non-stationarity
   978	threshold (1e-3) is unchanged for both.
   979	
   980	**A8.2 Anchors.** The tight and tighter anchors of every baseline configuration (both solvers) are the **native**
   981	QR-based Gauss–Newton at the tight (1e-7) and tighter (1e-8) levels: an adaptive solve to tolerance whose round-off floor
   982	is not squared. A1.7's "common LM solver at the tight level" is replaced. Distances and validity rules are unchanged.
   983	
   984	**A8.3 N-under ECSW ladder.** A support equal to r makes the weighted residual square, so its minimiser is an exact root
   985	and γ is round-off noise (every step non-stationary in the dry run); such a level can never be Q1-qualified. The ECSW
   986	ladder is therefore overdetermined: support caps $\{4r,\ 2r,\ \lceil1.25r\rceil\}$ (still far below the registered τ
   987	supports at real size). The Q-DEIM ladder is unchanged. The firing rule (A6.3) is unchanged.
