  1059	**A12.6 (code audit 6) Small-mesh G-pod and non-finite discrepancies.** The small-mesh G-pod reproduction test uses
  1060	the lane's `pod()` at rank $\rho_8=\#\{\sigma_i>10^{-8}\sigma_1\}$ (no cap) with tolerance 1e-6 relative: the
  1061	method of snapshots resolves singular values only above about $\sqrt{\epsilon}\,\sigma_1$, so A2.11's
  1062	$10^{-10}$/1e-8 reproduction is not attainable by the registered algorithm; the binding POD check is the production
  1063	certificate (A6.1), unchanged. Output discrepancies (timed vs scored) treat matching non-finite entries as agreement and
  1064	any mismatch of the non-finite pattern as non-finite, so an honestly invalid run reaches the invalid-run accounting
  1065	(A12.1) instead of an evidence error.
  1066	
  1067	**A12.7 (code audit 7) Timing outputs must be finite.** Every timed call's output and its scored comparison field must
  1068	be entirely finite (else the discrepancy is non-finite and acceptance fails); the NaN-aware agreement of A12.6 applies
  1069	only to the grid's invalid-run accounting.
  1070	
  1071	---
  1072	
  1073	## Amendment A13 (2026-10-18) — design audit 7 (`audits/codex-design-7.md`, NEEDS-RESTATEMENT, no WRONG)
  1074	
  1075	**A13.1 (A6.3 restated).** Rejecting ECSW ladder levels whose actual support is below r is a **registered
  1076	control-admissibility restriction** of this lane, not a consequence of the COMMON-BRIEF Q1 predicates (which test
  1077	stationarity, validity and distance, not uniqueness). The overdetermined ladder (A8.3) stands.
  1078	
  1079	**A13.2 (A8 restated).** The justification "Gauss–Newton converges quadratically, so the extra iteration is cheap" is
  1080	withdrawn (for non-zero-residual LSPG, Gauss–Newton is in general only linearly convergent with a residual-dependent
  1081	rate). The evidence is empirical: in the CPU dry run the native solver used 1 iteration per step at γ ≤ 1e-3 and 2 at
  1082	γ ≤ 1e-6, with rollout distances to the anchor of 2.4–3.3e-4 and about 1e-7 respectively; the cost of the setting is
  1083	measured in the smoke and in production (iteration counts are reported). Likewise, the failure of the square ECSW
  1084	support is an **observed dry-run outcome** (round-off-level residuals made γ noisy), not a general property of square
  1085	problems. These settings are frozen for production and are not relaxed after any verdict data.
  1086	
  1087	**A13.3 (A9 restated).** A9.1 is a **small-gradient backtracking-stall allowance**: an anchor step whose bounded line
  1088	search (eight halvings) is exhausted with a finite step is accepted when γ ≤ 100 gtol (effective limits 1e-5 tight,
  1089	1e-6 tighter). Round-off is the proposed explanation, not a proven one. Nominal steps (γ ≤ gtol) and allowance steps are
  1090	counted and reported separately for every anchor (`roundoff_stalls` counts the allowance steps). The COMMON-BRIEF Q1
  1091	bars are unchanged, including the tight/tighter agreement ≤ 2.5e-5.
  1092	
  1093	**A13.4 (A11 storage scope).** The field-and-trajectory retention of A11.2 is a **phase-I smoke** requirement. For
  1094	phase II the storage contract is registered in the phase-II release amendment: evidence is verified on the cluster in
  1095	the job (and by an offline checker on the pulled per-configuration summaries), only the selection-relevant fields
  1096	(Stage-B candidates and picks) are pulled, every pulled artifact is checksummed, and the local footprint is bounded by a
  1097	manifest-derived peak replacing §12's obsolete "≤ 2 GB per cell" statement. No required evidence is dropped silently.
  1098	
  1099	**A13.5 (job audit smk1-1) Smoke job mechanics.** The smoke driver runs under a hard `timeout` of the wall time minus
  1100	4 minutes, so the per-phase checkpointed evidence is always checksummed; caches (XDG, CUDA, JAX compilation) are
  1101	confined to the job directory; `smoke_accept.py` exits non-zero unless ALL passes, and "ALL-DONE" in the log means job
  1102	completion only. The staged config differs from the HEAD blob only by the added `commit` field (by design of
  1103	`stage.py`). Whether the full workload fits the hour is unproven; phases not reached are skipped and fail acceptance
  1104	(fail-closed), and the phase-I hand-back then reports exactly which controls were not demonstrated.
  1105	
